{"bag_of_words__cannot_be_used_as_a_feature_extractor_in__recurrent_neural_network_rnn_models_like_lstm_bilstm_gru_bigru": "The phrase \"cannot be used as a feature extractor in\" indicates a limitation or incompatibility of the bag of words method when applied to certain types of neural network models. Specifically, it highlights that the bag of words approach is not suitable for models that require the preservation of word order."},
{"recurrent_neural_network_rnn_models_like_lstm_bilstm_gru_bigru": "Recurrent neural network (RNN) models like LSTM, BiLSTM, GRU, and BiGRU are types of neural networks designed to handle sequential data. They are particularly effective in natural language processing tasks because they can maintain a form of memory over previous inputs in the sequence, which is crucial for understanding the context and order of words in text."},
{"order_of_words": "The order of words refers to the sequence in which words appear in a text. This sequence is crucial in understanding the context and meaning of sentences, especially in natural language processing tasks."},
