{"default_hyper_parameters": "Default hyper-parameters are the pre-set configurations used in machine learning models, which include settings like batch size and learning rate. In this context, traditional machine learning models use parameters from the sklearn library, while deep learning models use a batch size of 32 and a learning rate of 0.001."},
{"we__didn_t_do__any_hyperparameter_tuning_during_this_section": "The predicate \"didn\u2019t do\" indicates that the subject chose not to perform a certain action. In this context, it specifies that the researchers opted not to engage in a particular process during their study."},
{"any_hyperparameter_tuning_during_this_section": "The object \"any hyperparameter tuning during this section\" refers to the specific action that was not taken by the researchers. Hyperparameter tuning is the process of finding the optimal combination of hyperparameters for a machine learning model to achieve the best performance. In this case, the researchers did not adjust these parameters from their default values during the section of the study being discussed."},
{"default_hyper_parameters_for_traditional_machine_learning": "The default hyper-parameters for traditional machine learning refer to the standard settings used in various machine learning algorithms when no specific tuning is applied. These parameters are crucial as they determine the initial behavior and performance of the models."},
{"default_hyper_parameters_for_traditional_machine_learning__are_based_on__sklearn_library": "The phrase \"are based on\" indicates that the default hyper-parameters for traditional machine learning models are derived from or influenced by a specific source or framework. This relationship suggests that the parameters are not arbitrary but are instead grounded in established practices or libraries."},
{"sklearn_library": "The sklearn library, also known as scikit-learn, is a popular machine learning library in Python. It provides simple and efficient tools for data mining and data analysis, and it is widely used for its ease of use and comprehensive suite of algorithms. The library serves as a foundational resource for setting default hyper-parameters in traditional machine learning models.|Here is another description: The object is the Sklearn library, a comprehensive machine learning library in Python that provides simple and efficient tools for data mining and data analysis. It is widely used for training and evaluating machine learning models due to its extensive collection of algorithms and utilities.|Here is another description: The Sklearn library, also known as Scikit-learn, is a widely-used Python library for machine learning that provides simple and efficient tools for data mining and data analysis. It offers a range of algorithms for classification, regression, and clustering, among other tasks."},
{"we__consider__batch_size_32_and_learning_rate_0_001_as_default_hyper_parameters_for_the_deep_learning_models": "The predicate indicates the action or decision made by the subject. In this case, it refers to the consideration or selection of specific hyper-parameters for the deep learning models used in the study."},
{"batch_size_32_and_learning_rate_0_001_as_default_hyper_parameters_for_the_deep_learning_models": "The object describes the specific hyper-parameters that have been selected as default for the deep learning models. These include a batch size of 32 and a learning rate of 0.001, which are standard settings used in the absence of hyperparameter tuning."},
