{"gru__trained__deep_learning_models": "The term 'trained' in this context refers to the process of optimizing the parameters of the GRU model using a dataset. This involves adjusting the weights and biases of the model to minimize the difference between the predicted and actual outputs."},
{"bigru__trained__deep_learning_models": "The term \"trained\" in this context refers to the process of adjusting the parameters of the BiGRU model through a learning algorithm, using a dataset to optimize its performance in making predictions or classifications."},
{"ensemble_of_bigru_bilstm": "The Ensemble of (BiGRU+BiLSTM) is a combined deep learning model that integrates both Bidirectional Gated Recurrent Units (BiGRU) and Bidirectional Long Short-Term Memory (BiLSTM) architectures to leverage their respective strengths in sequence processing."},
{"ensemble_of_bigru_bilstm__trained__deep_learning_models": "The term \"trained\" refers to the process where the Ensemble of (BiGRU+BiLSTM) model undergoes learning from a dataset. During training, the model adjusts its parameters to minimize the difference between its predictions and the actual outcomes, thereby improving its performance on the given task."},
