{"cnn_model": "The CNN model is a type of deep learning model that was trained and evaluated using different architectures in the context of sentence classification."},
{"cnn_model__adopted__architecture_from_yoon_kim_s_paper": "The predicate \"adopted\" signifies that the CNN model utilized or incorporated a specific architecture as its foundational design. This action implies a direct implementation of pre-existing architectural principles into the model's structure."},
{"architecture_from_yoon_kim_s_paper": "The architecture from Yoon Kim\u2019s paper \"Convolutional Neural Networks for Sentence Classification\" is a specific design framework for CNNs that was proposed for the task of classifying sentences. This architecture was referenced and implemented in the CNN model discussed in the context."},
