{"paper__titled__convolutional_neural_networks_for_sentence_classification": "The predicate \"titled\" indicates that the paper has a specific title that identifies and describes its content and focus, which in this case is on the application of CNNs to sentence classification."},
{"convolutional_neural_networks_for_sentence_classification": "Yoon Kim's paper \"Convolutional Neural Networks for Sentence Classification\" presents a method using CNNs to classify sentences, aiming to enhance accuracy and efficiency in natural language processing tasks. The paper was presented at the 2014 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (EMNLP)."},
{"architecture": "The architecture refers to the specific configuration and arrangement of layers, nodes, and connections within a neural network model. In the context of deep learning, different architectures can significantly impact the performance and capabilities of the model."},
