{"tokenized_data": "Tokenized data refers to text that has been broken down into individual units called tokens, which are typically words or subwords. This process is essential for preparing text data for machine learning models, as it allows the model to process and understand the text in a structured format."},
{"tokenized_data__is_used_as__input_to_the_word_embedding_layer": "The phrase \"is used as\" indicates that the subject (tokenized data) serves a specific function or role within a system or process. In this context, it highlights the purpose of tokenized data in the subsequent stages of the machine learning pipeline."},
{"input_to_the_word_embedding_layer": "The input to the word embedding layer is the data that is fed into this specific layer of a neural network. The word embedding layer is responsible for converting the tokenized data into dense vector representations, which capture semantic meanings and relationships between words. This transformation is crucial for enabling the model to perform various natural language processing tasks effectively."},
{"output_of_the_word_embedding_layer": "The output of the word embedding layer is the result generated by the word embedding process, which transforms input tokens into dense vector representations."},
{"output_of_the_word_embedding_layer__is_sent_to__two_convolution_layers_parallelly": "The phrase \"is sent to\" indicates the directional flow of data from the word embedding layer to subsequent layers in the neural network architecture."},
{"two_convolution_layers_parallelly": "Two convolution layers operating in parallel are part of the neural network architecture, each using different kernel sizes (3\u00d73 and 5\u00d75) and followed by max pooling layers."},
{"one_convolution_layer": "One convolution layer is a component in a neural network architecture that processes input data through a series of mathematical operations to extract features. In this context, it is one of two parallel convolution layers that receive output from a word embedding layer."},
{"one_convolution_layer__uses_kernel_of_size__3_3": "The predicate \"uses kernel of size\" indicates the specific configuration of the convolution operation within the layer. It specifies the dimensions of the kernel, which is a small matrix used to apply filters to the input data, thereby detecting patterns such as edges or textures."},
{"another_convolution_layer": "Another convolution layer is a parallel processing unit that receives input from the word embedding layer. It operates alongside another convolution layer with a different kernel size."},
{"another_convolution_layer__uses_kernel_of_size__5_5": "The phrase \"uses kernel of size\" describes the specific configuration of the convolution layer, indicating the dimensions of the kernel it employs to process the input data."},
