{"10_folds_cross_validation": "10 folds cross-validation is a technique used in machine learning to evaluate the performance of a model. It involves dividing the dataset into 10 equal parts, or folds, and training the model on 9 of those folds while using the remaining fold for validation. This process is repeated 10 times, with each fold serving as the validation set once."},
