{"learning_rate_batch_size_and_number_of_epochs": "Learning rate, batch size, and number of epochs are hyper-parameters that play a crucial role in the training of deep learning models. The learning rate determines the step size at which the model updates its weights during training. The batch size refers to the number of training examples utilized in one iteration. The number of epochs is the number of times the entire training dataset is passed forward and backward through the neural network."},
