{"all_other_models": "\"All other models\" refers to a variety of alternative deep learning and traditional machine learning models that were evaluated alongside the ensemble model. These include standalone LSTM, CNN, BiGRU, BiLSTM, and CNN models, as well as various traditional machine learning approaches. Despite their respectable performance, none of these models matched the accuracy achieved by the ensemble model."},
{"ensemble_model_of_bilstm_and_bigru__has_accuracy_rate_of__87_66": "The phrase \"has accuracy rate of\" indicates the performance metric achieved by the ensemble model of BiLSTM and BiGRU. It signifies the percentage of correctly predicted instances out of the total instances in the test dataset, reflecting the model's effectiveness and reliability in the given task."},
{"87_66": "An accuracy rate of 87.66% represents the proportion of correct predictions made by the ensemble model of BiLSTM and BiGRU when evaluated on the test data. This high accuracy indicates that the model performs exceptionally well in classifying or detecting emotions in texts, outperforming other individual deep learning models and traditional machine learning models."},
{"other_deep_learning_models": "Other deep learning models refer to a variety of advanced machine learning techniques designed to process and analyze complex data structures, such as sequences and images, to achieve high-level abstractions and make accurate predictions or classifications.|Here is another description: Other deep learning models refer to various neural network architectures like LSTM, CNN, BiGRU, and BiLSTM that were evaluated alongside an ensemble model. These models are designed to process and classify data, particularly in the context of detecting emotions in texts.|Here is another description: Other deep learning models refer to various neural network architectures like LSTM, CNN, BiGRU, and BiLSTM that are used for complex pattern recognition tasks. These models are designed to learn representations of data with multiple levels of abstraction."},
