{"embedding_layer__is_initialized_using__pre_trained_word_embedding": "The phrase \"is initialized using\" indicates the process by which the embedding layer is set up before training. This involves loading pre-existing data or parameters into the layer to establish a starting point for the model's learning process."},
{"pre_trained_word_embedding": "Pre-trained word embeddings are pre-existing vector representations of words that have been trained on large corpora. These embeddings capture semantic and syntactic relationships between words, which can be leveraged to improve the performance of deep learning models by providing a rich initial representation for the embedding layer."},
{"we__performed__hyper_parameter_tuning": "The predicate \"performed\" indicates the action taken by the subject to carry out a specific task, in this case, the optimization of model parameters."},
{"hyper_parameter_tuning": "The object \"hyper-parameter tuning\" is the process of systematically adjusting the hyper-parameters of a machine learning model to find the optimal configuration that yields the best performance on a given dataset.|Here is another description: Hyper-parameter tuning is a process used to find the optimal settings for the parameters of a machine learning model that are not learned from the data, but rather set prior to training. It is crucial for improving the model's performance.|Here is another description: Hyper-parameter tuning is a process used in machine learning to find the best combination of hyper-parameters for a given model. It involves systematically searching through a range of possible values to determine which settings yield the best performance.|Here is another description: Hyper-parameter tuning is the process of selecting the optimal values for the configuration parameters of a machine learning model, which are not learned during the training process. These hyper-parameters can significantly impact the performance of the model, and therefore, careful tuning is essential to achieve the best results."},
