{"c": "The parameter C in the Support Vector Classifier is a regularization parameter that controls the trade-off between achieving a low error on the training data and minimizing the norm of the weights. It helps in preventing overfitting by penalizing the margin violations.|Here is another description: C is a parameter in the Support Vector Classifier, which influences the balance between maximizing the margin and minimizing the classification error.|Here is another description: C is a parameter in the Support Vector Classifier, which influences the trade-off between maximizing the margin and minimizing the classification error."},
