{"gamma": "Gamma is a parameter in the Support Vector Classifier that defines the influence of a single training example. Low values of gamma indicate a large influence, meaning that the decision boundary will be smooth; high values indicate a small influence, leading to a more complex, tightly fitted decision boundary.|Here is another description: Gamma is a parameter used in machine learning algorithms, particularly in Support Vector Machines (SVMs), to define the influence of single training examples. It plays a crucial role in determining the shape of the decision boundary in the feature space.|Here is another description: Gamma is a parameter used in machine learning algorithms, particularly in kernel methods like the Support Vector Classifier, to define the influence of a single training example. It plays a crucial role in determining the decision boundary's shape and complexity."},
