{"1_2": "The object \"1,2\" represents the possible values for the np parameter in the K-Neighbors Classifier. These values indicate that the number of neighbors considered by the algorithm can be either 1 or 2.|Here is another description: The object \"1,2\" represents the specific values assigned to the parameter 'p' in the K-Neighbors Classifier. These values determine the Minkowski distance metric used, where '1' corresponds to Manhattan distance and '2' to Euclidean distance."},
{"k_neighbors_classifier__has_leaf_size__29": "The 'has leaf size' predicate indicates a specific parameter setting within the K-Neighbors Classifier. This parameter influences how the algorithm groups data points into leaves during the construction of its decision tree.|Here is another description: The 'has leaf size' predicate indicates a specific parameter setting within the K-Neighbors Classifier. This parameter influences how the algorithm groups data points into clusters or 'leaves' during the classification process."},
