{"none_15_30": "The possible values for'max depth' in this context are None, 15, and 30. None implies no limit on the depth, allowing the tree to grow as deep as the data permits. The values 15 and 30 set specific limits on the depth, controlling the complexity and preventing overfitting.|Here is another description: The object 'None, 15, 30' represents the specific values that can be assigned to the maximum depth of a decision tree. 'None' implies no limit, while '15' and '30' are specific depth limits that can be set.|Here is another description: The possible values for 'max_depth' are None, 15, and 30. Setting 'max_depth' to None means there is no limit to the depth of the tree, while 15 and 30 represent specific limits to the tree depth, which can help in controlling overfitting and model complexity."},
